   "pages": [
    {
     "page": 1,
     "text": "LOPEZ ROSS AND WARREN CLINIC - DISCHARGE SUMMARY\n\nPatient: Jessica White DOB: 06/27/1972 Sex: F MRN: 522299\n\nAdmit: 09/30/2019 Discharge: 10/05/2019\n\nPrincipal diagnosis: Hepatitis C (SVR achieved; last tx 23.4 yrs ago)\nSecondary diagnoses: kidney stones; osteopenia\n\nHospital course: Ms. White was admitted on September 30, 2019, with a primary diagnosis of Hepatitis C, which was successfully treated with glecaprevir-pibrentasvir, achieving sustained virologic response (SVR) 23.4 years ago. During her hospitalization, she was also managed for secondary conditions including kidney stones and osteopenia. Her hospital course was uneventful, and she remained in stable condition throughout her stay. \n\nMs. White reported a history of back strain and was found to have a blood pressure of 142/88 mmHg and a weight of 171 lbs on her last visit on July 25, 2025. Previous visits showed varying weights and blood pressures, with the highest recorded pressure being 145/91 mmHg on December 22, 2022, and the highest weight of 181 lbs on April 29, 2022. \n\nShe has a family history significant for colon cancer in her father, who was diagnosed at age 48 and passed away at age 54, and type 2 diabetes in her mother, who was diagnosed at age 66 and passed away at age 76. \n\nProcedures: No specific procedures were performed during this admission. Management was primarily medical.\n\nDischarge medications:\n- Glecaprevir-pibrentasvir 100/40 mg for Hepatitis C (SVR achieved)\n- Tamsulosin 0.4 mg for kidney stones\n- Alendronate 70 mg for history: Ms. White currently uses cigars, with a frequency of 9 per year, starting from April 27, 2022. She consumes approximately one alcoholic drink per week.\n\nFollow-up: Ms. White is advised to follow up with her primary care physician for routine monitoring of her conditions. She should continue her current medications as prescribed and maintain regular follow-up appointments to monitor her Hepatitis C status, kidney stones, and osteopenia. \n\nThis discharge summary was prepared by Dr. Kenneth Vance, Family Lopez Ross and Warren Clinic. \n\n---\n\nPage 2\n\nLOPEZ ROSS AND WARREN CLINIC - DISCHARGE SUMMARY (CONTINUED)\n\nAdditional Ms. White's physical examination during her last visit was unremarkable except for the back strain. She denied any acute symptoms related to her Hepatitis C, kidney stones, or osteopenia. Her laboratory results were within normal limits, and she showed no signs of cirrhosis or other complications related to her Hepatitis C. \n\nShe was educated on the importance of adherence to her med"
    },
    {
     "page": 2,
     "text": "ication regimen and the potential risks associated with her social habits, including cigar use. \n\nIn summary, Ms. White was discharged home in stable condition a plan for continued outpatient management of her chronic conditions. \n\nPrepared by: Dr. Kenneth Vance, Family Medicine\nDate: October 5,\n"
    }
